{"id":"word:hebrew:H5787","type":"word","title":"עִוֵּר","subtitle":"H5787 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"blind (literally or figuratively)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to עִוֵּר (H5787) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: a.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 26 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"עִוֵּר (ʻivvêr) means blind (literally or figuratively) First listed occurrence: 2Sam 5 6."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"עִוֵּר","transliteration":"ʻivvêr","pronunciation":"iv-vare'","strong":"H5787","lemmaId":"hebrew:H5787","partOfSpeech":"a","forms":["עִוֵּר֙","עִוֵּ֣ר","עִוֵּ֔ר","עִוֵּ֖ר","עִוְרִ֗ים"],"morphs":[["HAamsa",11],["HAampa",6],["HTd/Aampa",2],["HRd/Aampa",2],["HTd/Aamsa",1],["HAafpa",1],["HC/Td/Aampa",1],["HC/Aamsa",1],["HRd/Aamsa",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"blind (literally or figuratively)","usage":"blind (men, people).","full":"H5787. ivver עִוֵּר adjective blind ; — only absolute ׳ע Exod 4:11 +, plural עִיְרִים 2Sam 5:6 +, feminine עִוְרוֺת Isa 42:7 ; (with article הָעִוֵּר Deut 28:29 , elsewhere ׳הַע Baer Ginsb; van d. H. לָעִוֵּר Job 29:15 , הָעִוְרִים 2Sam 5:6 , 8 ; Isa 42:18 ); &#8212; blind , usually as substantive = the blind: 1 literally, physically blind: a. of men Exod 4:11 (J; opposed to מִּקֵּחַ ), 2Sam 5:6 , 8 (twice in verse); Lev 19:14 (H), Deut 27:18 ; Jer 31:8 ; Job 29:15 ; in simile Deut 28:29 ; Zeph 1:17 ; Isa 59:10 , compare Lam 4:14 (apposition); as adjective attribute ע ׳אִישׁ Lev 21:18 (H). b. of sacrifice animal Deut 15:21 ; Mal 1:8 . 2 figurative, a. of the helpless, groping Isa 29:18 ; 35:5 ; 42:16 ; Psa 146:8 ; as adjective attribute, עִוְרוֺת עֵינַיִם Isa 42:7 . b. of the dull, unreceptive , Isa 42:18-19 , (3 t. in verse) (but 42:19 c read חֵרֵשׁ q. v.); as adjective attributive עִוֵּר עַם 43:8 ; as predicate 56:10 .","rootNote":"intensive from 5786 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew D